From 9db8bbfd2c8565ab96f542cfdd28637d3855d908 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: steamac <steamac@localhost>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 23:13:31 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 12/15] MSL: Location-based vertex payload between the
 GS-emulation stages

The payload between the object stage (vertex shader) and the mesh stage (geometry shader)
of an emulated geometry pipeline was the vertex shader's output struct on one side and a
struct built from the geometry shader's inputs on the other, so the two only matched if the
geometry shader read every vertex output, in order, with the same types. A geometry shader
reading a subset of the outputs read a shifted layout, and gl_in[] blocks (glslang, DXVK) did
not compile at all (undeclared gl_PerVertex, '.out.' member access, [[position]] on a
struct).

Use a layout independent of both shaders: per vertex, position, point size, clip and cull
distances, and one uint4 per location holding the bits of each component. The object stage
stores the vertex outputs by builtin / location / component; the mesh stage loads the
geometry inputs the same way, including the members of user blocks and of gl_in[] blocks.
Declare the gl_PerVertex struct of gl_in[] and access its members as plain struct members.
